From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aiueo52 <aiueo52@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:13:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 056/105] hc boundary: fold the combine apply into the next
 mix's K0 (SGLANG_HC_APPLY_MIX_FUSED)

The combine writes the branch residual and the next boundary's K0 reads it
straight back to norm it. K0's grid is one CTA per (row, branch) -- exactly
the slice the apply writes -- so the apply becomes K0's prologue: the CTA
reduces the gate partials for its branch, forms `residual + a * block_output`,
stores the new residual once, and carries it in registers into the sum of
squares. One kernel and one row round trip per boundary go away.

Wired through the existing `combine_then_mix` seam, so it covers the
attention->MoE boundary inside a layer (48 of the 96 target boundaries per
step); the layer->layer boundary still runs the standalone apply. The fused
path needs a gate from R1, K0 to exist, and one branch to fit one tile;
anything else falls back to combine + mix. Default off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
